        "date": "2026-11-13T01:47:34Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(mcp): set_part_axes aligns the full 3D frame from two axis picks\n\nset_part_axes now builds AlignPartToSetup::align_from_axes, the command\nthe Setups page's \"Part axes\" rows apply (#769). With one axis it falls\nback to the in-plane turn (#557) and still reports turn_deg; with both\n+Y and +X their 3D directions define the full frame (frame \"full_3d\"),\n+Z on the right-hand cross, so a left-handed pair is honoured as the GUI\ndoes instead of being refused. One undo step either way.\n\nPinned by mcp_align_axes::set_part_axes_with_both_axes_aligns_the_full_3d_frame.\nThe camcraft-mcp skill row is updated; PROCESS_VERSION 46.\n\nFixes #1329\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL",
